assist-plugin contains code and design patterns derived from the software-development
Claude plugin, authored by Toni-Jan Keith Monserrat.

The following components are adapted from software-development (paths are relative
to plugins/assist-plugin/):
- The six-step orchestration framework in skills/do/SKILL.md
- The routing table structure and debugging workflow in skills/debug/SKILL.md
- The agent roster naming and role taxonomy
- The reference file architecture (agent-registry, model-routing, plan-format, review-protocol)

These components were originally released under the MIT license and are included
here with modifications and improvements as documented in docs/TOKEN_OPTIMIZATION.md and
docs/ARCHITECTURE.md. The original MIT notice is reproduced at the end of this file.

Original work in assist-plugin (88% by volume):
- Complete documentation set (Claude.md, README.md, docs/*)
- Abstract model routing strategy with Haiku/Sonnet/Opus tiers
- Governance-gate review protocol with OWASP/coverage/sign-off gates
- Per-agent model override mechanism in the `do` skill
- New agents: code-reviewer, explore, general-purpose
- Compact agent-card format
- All supporting skills and their implementations

